  "_about": "The smooth relax law. Per iteration, F = strn/20; ring C(v) = edge neighbours, or only the border-edge neighbours when v is FLAGGED (on a border and > 2 neighbours); A = F*sum(P_i - P_v); D = sum|P_v - P_i|; c = 1, or for a flagged vertex with >= 2 border neighbours (mean |n_v.n_i|)^2 with n = unit(sum of first-corner polygon normals) of the ORIGINAL mesh in float; for each i in C: u = (P_v - P_i)*c/L_i, C_i = (L_i/D)(A - u(A.u)), force[v] += C_i, force[i] -= C_i; then P += force on ACTIVE vertices only. Positions stay double across iterations and are written as float once. Preserve: at iterations i < 10, i == iters-1 and every 100th, each active point is projected along -n_v onto the ORIGINAL surface (nearest hit on the line; no hit keeps the point). Falloff: weight at the original position, weight 0 = inactive, lerp(orig, result, w) last. Active = selection's vertices (polygon selection = all its vertices; none = whole mesh) minus locks minus weight 0; inactive vertices are fixed neighbours and receive no reaction; topology from the whole mesh. lockBound = any vertex on a border edge; lockCorner = used by exactly one polygon; lockSharp = both ends of an edge whose face normals dot below cos(sharpThreshold degrees), and it forces c = 1.",
